 PROJECT TODO - Doctor Management & Simple Appointment Booking System
================================================================================
 Generated: 2026-08-12
 Legend:  [x] Implemented   [~] Partially implemented   [ ] Not implemented

================================================================================
 1. USER ROLES
================================================================================
[x] Management (admin)     -> Role created in RolesAndPermissionsSeeder
[x] Doctor                 -> Role created in RolesAndPermissionsSeeder
[x] Regular User (patient) -> Role created in RolesAndPermissionsSeeder

================================================================================
 2. ADMIN CAPABILITIES
================================================================================
--- Specialty Management --------------------------------------------------------
[x] Add specialty          -> POST /api/v1/admin/specialties (SpecialtyController@store)
[x] Edit specialty         -> PUT/PATCH /api/v1/admin/specialties/{specialty}
[x] Delete specialty       -> DELETE /api/v1/admin/specialties/{specialty} (soft delete)

--- Doctor Management -----------------------------------------------------------
[x] View list of doctors   -> GET /api/v1/admin/doctors (AdminPanelDoctorManagement@index)
                              NOTE: uses ->get() (no pagination)
[~] Approve doctor         -> via generic status update (set status = active)
[~] Reject doctor          -> via generic status update (status = rejected; 'rejected' is in enum)
[~] Deactivate doctor      -> via generic status update (set status = suspended)
    -> All three are handled by a single endpoint:
       PUT/PATCH /api/v1/admin/doctors/{doctor} (UpdateDoctorStatusRequest)

--- Doctor Profile Editing (by admin) -------------------------------------------
[x] Edit specialty         -> PATCH/PUT /api/v1/admin/doctors/profile/{profile}
[x] Edit description (bio)
[x] Edit status
[~] Edit image             -> image is a plain string; NO real file upload/storage
[~] Profile list           -> GET .../profile uses paginate() (only paginated endpoint)

================================================================================
 3. DOCTOR CAPABILITIES
================================================================================
--- Registration ----------------------------------------------------------------
[x] Register               -> POST /api/v1/doctor/register
[x] Role assignment        -> assigns 'doctor' role (was 'admin'; fixed)
[x] Profile created        -> DoctorProfile with status = pending
[ ] Block panel until approved -> NOT enforced (no middleware/guard rejects a pending doctor)

--- Complete Profile ------------------------------------------------------------
[x] View own profile       -> GET /api/v1/doctor/profile/{profile} (policy: view + permission:profile.view)
[x] Update own profile     -> PATCH /api/v1/doctor/profile/{profile} (policy: update + permission:profile.update)
[x] Fields editable: mobile, medical_code, image (string), specialty_id, address,
    working_hours, bio
[~] Name                   -> lives on User model, no doctor endpoint to edit it

--- Appointment Management (doctor) ----------------------------------------------
[x] View appointments      -> GET /api/v1/doctor/appointment (permission:appointment.view)
[x] Approve appointment    -> PATCH /api/v1/doctor/appointment/{appointment} (permission:appointment.pending|cancel)
[x] Cancel appointment     -> same PATCH endpoint (status = canceled)
    -> ownership enforced via doctor_id (403 for non-owner)

================================================================================
 4. REGULAR USER (PATIENT) CAPABILITIES
================================================================================
[x] Register               -> POST /api/v1/register (patient role, auto-login; no approval)
[x] View approved doctors  -> GET /api/v1/patient/appointment (whereStatus 'active', permission:doctor.view)
                              NOTE: no pagination, no eager loading
[x] Book appointment       -> POST /api/v1/patient/appointment (auth:sanctum + permission:appointment.create)

================================================================================
 5. TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS
